title: Elections to the National Assembly
subtitle: Germany votes on 19 January.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 1 and spartacist_uprising_done = 1
max-visits: 1

= Elections to the National Assembly

Germany votes for a National Assembly that will write the new constitution, the first national election in which women can vote. Our founding congress voted to boycott it, against the Zentrale's advice.

- @boycott: Respect the congress and boycott the election.
- @candidates: Overrule the congress and stand candidates where we can.
- @vote_uspd: Tell workers to vote for the USPD.

@boycott
subtitle: The congress decided; the Zentrale obeys.
on-arrival: ultraleft_satisfaction += 5; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5; worker_support -= 2

Our posters call on workers to stay away. Most vote anyway, for the SPD and the USPD.

@candidates
subtitle: [? if lock_elections = 1 : Against the party line: costs 10 Unity. ?] Overruling a congress costs a further 10 Unity, and it is very late to register lists.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_name +] line forbids taking part in bourgeois elections.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_elections == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.unity -= 10;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 20;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.election_boycott = 0;
!}

Our lists appear in a handful of constituencies. We win few votes, but a principle has been set: the Zentrale, not the congress, has the last word. The districts will remember.

@vote_uspd
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs 10 Unity. ?] Helps the Independents; the ultra-left is appalled.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_name +] line forbids any support for social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.uspd_relation += 12;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10;
!}

The Independents gain votes in the workers' districts, and they know whom to thank.
